---
export const prerender = true;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<title>Your Shopify Store Owner Handbook — Cornerstone Services, Inc.</title>
<meta name="description" content="A calm, plain-English training guide for running your Shopify store day to day. Built by Cornerstone Services, Inc. (CRST)." />
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:opsz,wght@9..144,400;9..144,500;9..144,600;9..144,700&family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,400;9..40,500;9..40,600;9..40,700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --bg:        #FAF6EE;
    --bg-soft:   #F2EBDA;
    --ink:       #14213D;
    --ink-soft:  #3A4763;
    --muted:     #6B7589;
    --line:      #E3DAC2;
    --brass:     #B8893A;
    --brass-dim: #8E6926;
    --cream:     #FFFBF3;
    --shadow:    0 1px 0 rgba(20,33,61,.04), 0 24px 60px -28px rgba(20,33,61,.18);
    --radius:    14px;
  }

  *,*::before,*::after { box-sizing: border-box }
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100% }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: 'DM Sans', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1vw + 11px, 17px);
    line-height: 1.65;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
  }
  ::selection { background: var(--brass); color: var(--cream) }

  /* TOP RIBBON */
  .ribbon {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--cream);
    font-size: .78rem;
    letter-spacing: .16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-align: center;
    padding: .6rem 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* HEADER */
  header.masthead { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--cream) }
  .masthead-inner {
    max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.2rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem;
  }
  .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .85rem; text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink) }
  .brand img { height: 42px; width: auto; display: block }
  .brand-text { display: flex; flex-direction: column; line-height: 1.15 }
  .brand-text .name { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.05rem; letter-spacing: -.01em }
  .brand-text .sub { font-size: .72rem; color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase }
  .masthead nav { display: flex; gap: 1.4rem; font-size: .85rem }
  .masthead nav a { color: var(--ink-soft); text-decoration: none; transition: color .2s }
  .masthead nav a:hover { color: var(--brass) }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .masthead nav { display: none } }

  /* HERO */
  .hero {
    max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 5.5rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: .74rem; letter-spacing: .22em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brass); font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
    padding: .4rem .9rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--brass);
    border-radius: 999px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.2vw, 4.4rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -.025em;
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  h1 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--brass); font-weight: 500 }
  .hero-lede {
    max-width: 640px; margin: 0 auto;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.6vw, 1.2rem);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .hero-meta {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 2rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: .78rem; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
  }
  .hero-meta span { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .5rem }
  .hero-meta span::before { content: ""; width: 6px; height: 6px; background: var(--brass); border-radius: 50% }

  /* REASSURANCE */
  .reassurance {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--cream);
    padding: 5rem 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .reassurance::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 40% at 80% 20%, rgba(184,137,58,.18), transparent 60%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 50% 50% at 10% 90%, rgba(184,137,58,.10), transparent 60%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .reassurance-inner { max-width: 880px; margin: 0 auto; position: relative }
  .reassurance .eyebrow { color: #E6C176; border-color: rgba(230,193,118,.4); background: rgba(230,193,118,.06) }
  .reassurance h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.6vw, 2.8rem);
    line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -.02em;
    margin: .5rem 0 1.6rem;
  }
  .reassurance h2 em { font-style: italic; color: #E6C176; font-weight: 500 }
  .reassurance p { font-size: 1.06rem; color: rgba(255,251,243,.85); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 1.2rem }
  .reassurance .pillars {
    margin-top: 2.5rem; display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(170px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .pillar {
    border: 1px solid rgba(230,193,118,.22);
    padding: 1.1rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: rgba(255,251,243,.03);
  }
  .pillar .num { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-size: 1.3rem; color: #E6C176; display: block; margin-bottom: .3rem }
  .pillar .label { font-size: .85rem; color: rgba(255,251,243,.78); line-height: 1.45 }

  /* TOC */
  .toc-wrap { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 1.5rem 1rem }
  .toc-wrap h3 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-weight: 500;
    font-size: .85rem; letter-spacing: .2em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }
  .toc {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: .4rem 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding-top: 1.2rem;
  }
  .toc a {
    display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: .9rem;
    padding: .6rem 0;
    color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px dotted transparent;
    transition: border-color .2s, color .2s;
  }
  .toc a:hover { color: var(--brass); border-bottom-color: var(--brass) }
  .toc a .n { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-style: italic; color: var(--brass); font-size: .95rem; min-width: 24px }
  .toc a .t { font-size: .95rem }

  /* MODULES */
  main.modules { max-width: 880px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1.5rem 4rem }
  .module { padding: 4rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line) }
  .module:last-child { border-bottom: none }
  .module-head { margin-bottom: 2rem }
  .module-num {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-style: italic;
    color: var(--brass); font-size: 1rem; letter-spacing: .04em;
    display: block; margin-bottom: .6rem;
  }
  .module h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.4vw, 2.5rem);
    line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -.02em;
    margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--ink);
  }
  .module .intro { font-size: 1.08rem; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 1.6rem }
  .module p { margin: 0 0 1.2rem; color: var(--ink-soft) }

  /* VIDEO CARD */
  .video-card {
    background: var(--cream);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }
  .video-frame { position: relative; width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 16/9; background: #000 }
  .video-frame iframe { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0 }
  .video-caption {
    padding: 1rem 1.3rem 1.1rem;
    font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted);
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .video-caption strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500 }

  /* KEY POINTS */
  .key-points {
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--brass);
    padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem;
    border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }
  .key-points h4 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-weight: 600;
    font-size: .85rem; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--brass-dim); margin: 0 0 .9rem;
  }
  .key-points ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; color: var(--ink) }
  .key-points li { margin-bottom: .5rem; line-height: 1.55 }
  .key-points li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0 }

  /* SOPs */
  .sops {
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    padding: 5rem 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .sops-inner { max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto }
  .sops .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 1rem }
  .sops h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.4vw, 2.6rem);
    line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: -.02em;
    margin: 0 0 .8rem;
  }
  .sops p.lede { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 640px; margin: 0 0 2.5rem }
  .sop-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1.3rem }
  .sop-card {
    background: var(--cream);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.8rem 1.8rem 1.5rem;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
  }
  .sop-card h3 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.35rem; margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .7rem;
  }
  .sop-card h3::before { content: ""; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--brass) }
  .sop-card ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.2rem; color: var(--ink-soft) }
  .sop-card ol li { margin-bottom: .7rem; line-height: 1.5 }
  .sop-card .freq { font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: .4rem }

  /* CLOSING */
  .closing { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 5rem 1.5rem 3rem; text-align: center }
  .closing h2 {
    font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-weight: 500; font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    line-height: 1.25; color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
  }
  .closing p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7 }
  .signature { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; font-style: italic; color: var(--brass); font-size: 1.05rem }

  /* FOOTER */
  footer { background: var(--ink); color: rgba(255,251,243,.78); padding: 3rem 1.5rem 2rem }
  .footer-inner {
    max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; gap: 2rem; flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .footer-brand { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .6rem; max-width: 340px }
  .footer-brand img { height: 36px; width: auto; filter: brightness(0) invert(1); opacity: .92 }
  .footer-brand p { font-size: .85rem; line-height: 1.55; color: rgba(255,251,243,.65); margin: 0 }
  .footer-meta { font-size: .78rem; color: rgba(255,251,243,.55); line-height: 1.7; text-align: right }
  .footer-meta strong { color: rgba(255,251,243,.85); font-weight: 500; display: block; margin-bottom: .3rem; letter-spacing: .04em }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .footer-inner { flex-direction: column }
    .footer-meta { text-align: left }
  }

  /* ENTRANCE ANIMATION */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .fade-in { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(12px); animation: fade .9s cubic-bezier(.22,.61,.36,1) forwards }
    .hero .eyebrow { animation-delay: .05s }
    .hero h1 { animation-delay: .15s }
    .hero-lede { animation-delay: .3s }
    .hero-meta { animation-delay: .45s }
  }
  @keyframes fade { to { opacity: 1; transform: none } }

  /* LINKS */
  a.inline { color: var(--brass-dim); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--brass); transition: color .2s, border-color .2s }
  a.inline:hover { color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink) }

  strong { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink) }
  .quiet { color: var(--muted) }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="ribbon">A Practical Handbook for Running Your Shopify Store</div>

<header class="masthead">
  <div class="masthead-inner">
    <a class="brand" href="#top">
      <img src="/images/crst-logo.webp" alt="Cornerstone Services, Inc." />
      <span class="brand-text">
        <span class="name">Cornerstone Services, Inc.</span>
        <span class="sub">Training &amp; Operations</span>
      </span>
    </a>
    <nav>
      <a href="#how-it-works">How It Works</a>
      <a href="#modules">Modules</a>
      <a href="#sops">Daily &amp; Weekly</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="hero" id="top">
  <span class="eyebrow fade-in">Your Store Owner Handbook</span>
  <h1 class="fade-in">Run your Shopify store with <em>confidence</em>, not anxiety.</h1>
  <p class="hero-lede fade-in">A plain‑English walkthrough of everything you actually need: the dashboard, products, orders, payments, shipping, and the simple rhythm of daily and weekly tasks. No code. No jargon. Just the parts that matter.</p>
  <div class="hero-meta fade-in">
    <span>7 Short Modules</span>
    <span>Curated Videos</span>
    <span>Daily &amp; Weekly SOPs</span>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="reassurance" id="how-it-works">
  <div class="reassurance-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">Start Here · Read This First</span>
    <h2>Your store is custom on the outside. <em>Standard Shopify on the inside.</em></h2>
    <p>This is the single most important thing to understand before anything else, and it's the thing that will quietly answer most of the worries you might have about your store.</p>
    <p>Your storefront — the part your customers see when they visit your website — was custom built for you. It's faster and more polished than a typical Shopify theme. But <strong>behind the scenes, your store runs on Shopify itself</strong>, the same platform that powers more than a million online businesses worldwide.</p>
    <p>That means everything that matters is handled by tools that have been tested, refined, and trusted for years:</p>
    <div class="pillars">
      <div class="pillar"><span class="num">1</span><span class="label">Products live in Shopify</span></div>
      <div class="pillar"><span class="num">2</span><span class="label">Orders process through Shopify</span></div>
      <div class="pillar"><span class="num">3</span><span class="label">Payments run through Shopify</span></div>
      <div class="pillar"><span class="num">4</span><span class="label">Inventory tracks in Shopify</span></div>
      <div class="pillar"><span class="num">5</span><span class="label">Customer data sits in Shopify</span></div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:2rem">Think of it this way: <strong>Shopify is the engine. Your custom site is the bodywork.</strong> Everything safe, proven, and reliable about Shopify is still doing the heavy lifting underneath — you just got a much nicer car wrapped around it.</p>
    <p>So when you log into your Shopify admin (Module 1 below), you're working with the same tool every other Shopify merchant uses. Same buttons. Same flows. Same support. <strong>Every video in this handbook was made for regular Shopify users — and it applies directly to your store.</strong></p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="toc-wrap" id="modules">
  <h3>What's Inside</h3>
  <nav class="toc">
    <a href="#m1"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">Your Shopify Dashboard</span></a>
    <a href="#m2"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">Managing Products</span></a>
    <a href="#m3"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">Orders &amp; Checkout</span></a>
    <a href="#m4"><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">Getting Paid (Shopify Payments)</span></a>
    <a href="#m5"><span class="n">05</span><span class="t">Shipping &amp; Fulfillment</span></a>
    <a href="#m6"><span class="n">06</span><span class="t">Customer Notifications</span></a>
    <a href="#m7"><span class="n">07</span><span class="t">Abandoned Cart Recovery</span></a>
    <a href="#sops"><span class="n">08</span><span class="t">Daily &amp; Weekly SOPs</span></a>
  </nav>
</div>

<main class="modules">

  <section class="module" id="m1">
    <div class="module-head">
      <span class="module-num">Module 01</span>
      <h2>Your Shopify Dashboard</h2>
      <p class="intro">The dashboard (Shopify calls it the "admin") is your command center. Once you know your way around the left‑hand sidebar, you can run the entire store from here.</p>
    </div>
    <p>Start by getting comfortable with where things live. You don't need to click into every option on day one — just know that the sections you'll use most are <strong>Orders</strong>, <strong>Products</strong>, and <strong>Customers</strong>, all near the top of the sidebar.</p>

    <div class="video-card">
      <div class="video-frame">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Oqcww4vLUnM" title="Shopify Admin Essentials || Shopify Academy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe>
      </div>
      <div class="video-caption">
        <span><strong>Shopify Admin Essentials</strong> · Official Shopify Academy</span>
        <span>Watch</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="key-points">
      <h4>What to remember</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>The sidebar on the left is how you navigate — <strong>Home, Orders, Products, Customers, Analytics, Marketing, Discounts</strong>.</li>
        <li>Click the gear icon (Settings, bottom‑left) for store‑wide settings: shipping, taxes, payments, notifications.</li>
        <li>The top search bar finds orders, products, and customers fast — use it instead of scrolling.</li>
        <li>The Shopify mobile app gives you the same dashboard on your phone. Useful for checking orders on the go.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="module" id="m2">
    <div class="module-head">
      <span class="module-num">Module 02</span>
      <h2>Managing Products</h2>
      <p class="intro">Adding products is the most frequent task you'll do. Once you've done it three or four times, it becomes muscle memory.</p>
    </div>
    <p>For each product, you'll fill in a title, description, photos, price, and inventory count. Shopify automatically makes the product show up on your storefront once you save it as <strong>Active</strong>. If you want to hide a product, switch it to <strong>Draft</strong> — it stays in your system, just not visible to customers.</p>

    <div class="video-card">
      <div class="video-frame">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/r_9qBZUZ_XQ" title="How to Add a Product — Shopify Help Center" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe>
      </div>
      <div class="video-caption">
        <span><strong>How to Add a Product</strong> · Official Shopify Help Center walkthrough</span>
        <span>Watch</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="key-points">
      <h4>Product checklist</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Title</strong> — clear and descriptive (e.g. "Brushed Cotton Throw — Forest Green").</li>
        <li><strong>Description</strong> — what it is, who it's for, why it's good. A few short paragraphs is plenty.</li>
        <li><strong>Photos</strong> — at least 3. The first photo is the one customers see in the catalog.</li>
        <li><strong>Price</strong> — required. "Compare at" price shows a strikethrough sale price if you want one.</li>
        <li><strong>Inventory</strong> — turn on "Track quantity" if you have a fixed stock; Shopify will warn you when it runs low.</li>
        <li><strong>Status</strong> — Active (visible) or Draft (hidden). Set to Active when ready.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="module" id="m3">
    <div class="module-head">
      <span class="module-num">Module 03</span>
      <h2>Orders &amp; Checkout</h2>
      <p class="intro">This is usually the most worrying part for new store owners — and the part Shopify handles best. Here's what actually happens when a customer buys something.</p>
    </div>
    <p>A customer adds a product to their cart, clicks checkout, fills in their address, and pays. Shopify takes the payment, sends them a confirmation email, and creates an order in your dashboard. <strong>You don't have to do anything for the order to appear</strong> — it just shows up under the Orders tab, ready for you to fulfill.</p>
    <p>Most stores get a notification too (email or mobile push) the moment an order comes in. We'll cover those notifications in Module 6.</p>

    <div class="video-card">
      <div class="video-frame">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/8FwU8Ps3DMY" title="How To Fulfill Orders On Shopify 2025 — Step-by-Step Tutorial" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe>
      </div>
      <div class="video-caption">
        <span><strong>How To Fulfill Orders On Shopify</strong> · Step-by-step for beginners (2025)</span>
        <span>Watch</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="key-points">
      <h4>The order flow in plain English</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Customer pays</strong> → order appears in your <em>Orders</em> tab with status "Unfulfilled".</li>
        <li><strong>You pack the item</strong> and print the shipping label (Module 5 covers this).</li>
        <li><strong>You click "Mark as Fulfilled"</strong> in Shopify — this triggers an automatic shipping email to the customer.</li>
        <li><strong>Order status updates to "Fulfilled"</strong> and you're done.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="module" id="m4">
    <div class="module-head">
      <span class="module-num">Module 04</span>
      <h2>Getting Paid — Shopify Payments</h2>
      <p class="intro">Shopify Payments is the built‑in payment processor. It accepts credit cards, debit cards, Apple Pay, Google Pay, and Shop Pay. The money goes from the customer's card to your bank account on a regular schedule — usually a few business days.</p>
    </div>
    <p>You'll connect your business bank account once during setup. After that, Shopify handles every transaction automatically. You can see every payment, fee, and payout under <strong>Settings → Payments</strong> and <strong>Finances → Payouts</strong>.</p>

    <div class="video-card">
      <div class="video-frame">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/cSf77ssKzfI" title="Setting Up Payments || Shopify Academy" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe>
      </div>
      <div class="video-caption">
        <span><strong>Setting Up Payments</strong> · Official Shopify Academy</span>
        <span>Watch</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="key-points">
      <h4>What to know about payments</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Transaction fees</strong> — Shopify Payments charges a small percentage per sale (typically 2.4–2.9% + 30¢). This is normal and built into your price.</li>
        <li><strong>Payouts</strong> — money lands in your bank account on a rolling schedule (you can see exactly when under "Payouts").</li>
        <li><strong>Refunds</strong> — issued in two clicks from inside the order. The customer gets their money back to the same card.</li>
        <li><strong>Chargebacks</strong> — rare, but Shopify will email you if one happens. Don't panic; there's a simple process to respond.</li>
        <li>If you ever want to also accept PayPal or another method, that gets added under <em>Settings → Payments</em>.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="module" id="m5">
    <div class="module-head">
      <span class="module-num">Module 05</span>
      <h2>Shipping &amp; Fulfillment</h2>
      <p class="intro">Once an order comes in, you ship it. Shopify can buy and print shipping labels for you (USPS, UPS, DHL) at discounted rates — no need to drive to the post office for label paperwork.</p>
    </div>
    <p>You'll set your shipping rates once under <strong>Settings → Shipping and Delivery</strong>. Most stores use a flat rate or weight‑based rate per package. Once that's done, every customer sees the right shipping cost automatically at checkout.</p>

    <div class="video-card">
      <div class="video-frame">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/VB6HcbDx1Bg" title="How to setup Shopify Shipping || Shopify Help Center" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen loading="lazy"></iframe>
      </div>
      <div class="video-caption">
        <span><strong>How to Set Up Shopify Shipping</strong> · Official Shopify Help Center</span>
        <span>Watch</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="key-points">
      <h4>Shipping in three steps</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Buy the label</strong> directly from inside the order in Shopify.</li>
        <li><strong>Print it</strong> on a regular printer or thermal label printer, and tape it to the package.</li>
        <li><strong>Click "Mark as fulfilled"</strong> — Shopify auto‑emails the tracking number to the customer.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="module" id="m6">
    <div class="module-head">
      <span class="module-num">Module 06</span>
      <h2>Customer Notifications</h2>
      <p class="intro">Shopify automatically sends professional, branded emails to customers at every step of the order. You don't have to write them or send them — they just happen.</p>
    </div>
    <p>Order confirmation, shipping confirmation, delivery confirmation, refund notice — all of it is automated. You can customize the wording or branding under <strong>Settings → Notifications</strong> if you ever want to, but the defaults are perfectly fine to start.</p>

    <div class="key-points">
      <h4>Notifications worth knowing</h4>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Order confirmation</strong> — sent the moment a customer pays.</li>
        <li><strong>Shipping confirmation</strong> — sent when you click "Mark as fulfilled" (includes tracking).</li>
        <li><strong>Out for delivery / delivered</strong> — sent automatically by the carrier integration.</li>
        <li><strong>Refund notification</strong> — sent when you issue a refund.</li>
        <li><em>You</em> will also receive an email (and mobile push, if you have the Shopify app) for every new order.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="module" id="m7">
    <div class="module-head">
      <span class="module-num">Module 07</span>
      <h2>Abandoned Cart Recovery <span class="quiet" style="font-size:1rem;font-style:italic"> · for later</span></h2>
      <p class="intro">An "abandoned cart" is when a customer adds something to their cart, starts checkout, then leaves before paying. About 70% of all carts get abandoned everywhere — it's normal. Shopify can automatically email those customers a gentle reminder.</p>
    </div>
    <p>This isn't something to set up on day one. Get comfortable with the basics first. But when you're ready (a few weeks in), this single feature can recover meaningful revenue with almost no effort.</p>

    <div class="video-card">
      <div class="video-frame">
        <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/Mw7FDcP9hh0" title="How to Set Up Shopify Abandoned Cart Email Automation" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture" allowfullscreen></iframe>
      </div>
      <div class="video-caption">
        <span><strong>Shopify Abandoned Cart — Free Built-in Setup</strong> · Marketing Automations walkthrough</span>
        <span>Watch</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="key-points">
      <h4>Bookmark for later</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>Found under <strong>Marketing → Automations</strong> in your Shopify admin.</li>
        <li>Shopify provides a free built‑in abandoned cart email template — turn it on and it's running.</li>
        <li>A typical setup: one reminder email 1 hour after abandonment, a second 24 hours later.</li>
        <li>Expect to recover roughly 5–15% of abandoned carts once the automation is on.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

<section class="sops" id="sops">
  <div class="sops-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">Module 08</span>
    <h2>Your Daily &amp; Weekly Rhythm</h2>
    <p class="lede">The whole platform can feel overwhelming until you settle into a simple routine. These two short checklists are the only thing you really need to keep the store healthy.</p>
    <div class="sop-grid">
      <div class="sop-card">
        <div class="freq">Daily — 10 to 15 minutes</div>
        <h3>Every Morning</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Open Shopify and check the <strong>Orders</strong> tab for anything new.</li>
          <li>Fulfill any unfulfilled orders — print labels, pack, ship.</li>
          <li>Reply to any new customer emails or messages.</li>
          <li>Glance at <strong>Home</strong> for today's sales and visitor count.</li>
          <li>Spot‑check inventory on best‑sellers (low‑stock warnings appear automatically).</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="sop-card">
        <div class="freq">Weekly — 30 to 45 minutes</div>
        <h3>Once a Week</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Review the <strong>Analytics</strong> tab — what sold, what didn't.</li>
          <li>Add any new products or update existing ones.</li>
          <li>Restock items running low (or mark them sold out).</li>
          <li>Check <strong>Finances → Payouts</strong> to confirm money is landing correctly.</li>
          <li>Review any abandoned checkouts and take note of patterns.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

